cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its accompanying proofs, please cite this release."
title: "The Sublinear Pair-Contraction Conjecture for Directed Hamiltonian Cycle and Its Lean-Checked Implication for P versus NP"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: ll3me
    website: "https://github.com/ll3me"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: 2026-11-26
url: "https://github.com/ll3me/mobius-lean/releases/tag/v0.2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ll3me/mobius-lean"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  The sublinear pair-contraction conjecture for directed Hamiltonian cycle
  remains open. It asserts that at every sufficiently large even vertex
  count n, some minimum-size AND/OR/NOT circuit with unrestricted sharing
  admits k(n) = o(n) disjoint oriented pairs on which the fixed simplifier
  R+ deletes at least 1% of the gates. The remaining circuit must decide
  every graph on n − k(n) vertices. Lean 4 proves that if this conjecture
  holds, then NP ⊈ P/poly and P ≠ NP. The formal proof
  also covers a vanishing saved fraction when the saving relative to the
  fraction of vertices removed grows without bound. The accompanying
  notes relate the numerical recurrence to rapid variation of positive
  sequences. Sources for rapid variation are Djurčić, Kočinac and Žižović
  (2007, DOI 10.1016/j.jmaa.2006.05.024) and Timotić, Djurčić and Kočinac
  (2022, Definition 2, DOI 10.2298/AADM181107003T).
